# The CFD solve screens, one solve that does the drag table and the 3D angles: in progress at a drag node, cancelled with its solved points
# on offer, the idle screen with the one action, finished with its provenance, in progress at an angle node, cancelled in the angles with
# the Mach numbers solved at both angles on offer. A real solve takes minutes and the driver waits for running tasks, so the solves are
# scripted (`analyze/solve_demo.rs`: the same events the worker sends, made-up numbers; the real stream is covered by the ignored tests
# of `analyze/cfd/tests`):
#   ICED_TEST_BACKEND=wgpu BOWSHOCK_CFD_DEMO=mid,done,flow3d-mid,mid cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/cfd-progress.drive out/cfd-progress
viewport 1300x800
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-drag-node-dark.png

# Cancel with four points solved: the points are on offer.
click "Cancel"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-stopped-dark.png

# Discard: the idle screen, the one action (Re-solve) and the option to leave the 3D angles out.
click "Discard"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot idle-dark.png

# A whole solve, finished: the summary row and the provenance.
click "Re-solve"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-done-dark.png

# The same solve in progress at an angle node (the drag table is in; `flow3d-mid` shows the 3D fixture flow at it, `angle-mid` has none), then cancelled in the angles: the Mach numbers with both angles are on offer.
click "Re-solve"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-angle-node-dark.png
click "Cancel"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-angles-stopped-dark.png
click "Keep 10 points · 3D at 4 Mach"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-angles-kept-dark.png

# The same mid-solve screen in the light theme.
click "Re-solve"
click "Prefs"
click "Light"
click "Done"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-mid-light.png
